shape theory.dimension.generator : theory.dimension {
  type: definition
  layer: 0
  """
// Definition 8.1 (Generator).
// A generator is an independent direction along which structure
// can be encoded in a shape system. Applying a generator produces
// a chain of shapes, each in contact with neighbors along that
// direction.
//
// Definition 8.2 (Dimensionality).
// The dimensionality of a shape system is the number of independent
// generators. Each generator contributes one dimension.
//
// A system with one generator is one-dimensional (a chain).
// Two generators: two dimensions (a lattice).
// Three generators: three dimensions (a 3D lattice).
// No upper limit: any number of generators is structurally valid.
// The number of generators N is not derived from the axiom. By
// Landscape Completeness, every coherent value of N persists.
//
// Derives from: theory.dimension
  """
}
